#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# negative_reals

#% text
# `negative_reals` is the domain of the real numbers less than 0, for facts `element(x, negative_reals)` in `assuming` and `refine`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `element(x, negative_reals)` with a number `x` is decided at once: `true` or `false`. With a symbol it is a fact that `assuming` adds to the assumptions.

#% item
# Functions that use assumptions (`simplify`, `refine`, `power_expand` and the sign tests) take the domain into account.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
element(-pi, negative_reals)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(-0.5, negative_reals)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(0, negative_reals)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
element(1, negative_reals)
#% output
#= false

#% text
# A symbol in the domain:

#% cell
assuming(element(x, negative_reals), simplify(sqrt(x^2)))
#% output
#= -x

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
assuming(element(x, negative_reals), refine(abs(x)))
#% output
#= -x

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A symbol alone is not decided:

#% cell
element(x, negative_reals)
#% output
#= element(x, reals) and x < 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `element`, `assuming`, `refine`, `reals`
